    "result": "I implemented both functions in `solution.py` and wrote a 57-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with all 57 tests green. `can_book` runs the spec's checks in order: the two `ValueError` checks first, then the same-day, four-hour and opening-hours rules, and finally the buffered conflict test. The conflict test lives in a small helper, `_conflicts`, which keeps `can_book`'s complexity low for the CRAP gate. `merge_intervals` validates every interval, sorts a copy of the input, and merges overlapping or touching pairs by extending the end with `max`. I did not measure line coverage, CRAP, mutation score or bandit locally, because the only shell command I was allowed was the test run. The tests exercise every branch and boundary in the spec (exact 4-hour and open/close edges, back-to-back bookings, buffer edges, unsorted and contained intervals, non-mutation of the input), so I expect the gates to pass, but that is unverified.",
